Porting Notes
=============

Below is a list of some of the changes made to get DHS to compile
with gcc-3.2.1 under RedHat-7.2. 

(Most of the non-trivial changes are commented with the string "XXX allan")


* Changed the syntax for standard #include files from:
  <file.h> to <file> (for C++) and <cfile> for C.
  
  For example: change <iostream.h> to <iostream> and
  change <stdio.h> to <cstdio>.

  The Standard C++ Header files are:

     algorithm bitset complex deque exception fstream functional
     iomanip ios iosfwd iostream istream iterator limits list locale map
     memory new numeric ostream queue set sstream stack stdexcept streambuf
     typeinfo utility valarray vector

  The Standard C Header files are:
 
     assert ctype errno float iso646 limits locale math setjmp signal
     stdarg stddef stdio stdlib string time


* Added std:: namespace prefix to all standard C++ names.
  (For example: std::iostream, std::string, std::list, std::endl).


* Replaced gets() with fgets(), tmpnam and tempnam with a new
  utility routine (gen_tempnam()), mktemp() with mkstemp(), 
  since gcc complains about these.


* Replaced some #ifdef solaris/#ifdef hpux code with configure based
  variables and code blocks. 

* Fixed portability and "out of date" problems with mnttab.h/mntent.h
  (media mounting code).

* Added #ifdef code to handle system specific calls, such as fork1()

* Replaced calls to "fusage()" with "statvfs()"

* Fixed a number of problems with varargs/stdargs usage

* Added numerous casts to please the compiler

* Changed some methods from private to public as required by the compiler

* Replaced lots of NULLs with 0s, as required by the compiler.

* Fixed a number of obvious bugs that were missed by previous compilers

* For the Linux port, had to compile some EPICS libraries from the sources
  (not all will compile, but enough to get DHS to compile)

* Updated outdated CFITSIO code usage (fits_set_mem_buff, etc.)

* Replaced list.erase() with list.clear() (erase was no longer defined)

* Had to replace the null first arg to attribute.info() with a dummy parameter
  in numerous places, to please the compiler

* Replaced heder file <strstream> with <sstream>
* Replaced ostrstream with ostringstream (ostrstream is deprecated)
* Same for istrstream (istringstream)
  (Note that ostringstream is not compatible, so code changes were
   needed)

* Changed process thread id init values to 0, from -1 (type is unsigned)


Other Changes
=============

The following changes were not required for compiling, but for running:

* Pass a non-null (pthread_t) argument as first arg to pthread_create()

* In the call to the cfitsio routine 'fits_read_key', replaced 'boolean'
  &hasExtended with 'int', since bool is no one byte, and an int is 
  expected. Since the address is passed and the object is written to, 
  the following 3 bytes get clobbered is a one-byte bool is passed!

* Added a call to "((cMutex *) dcdPMutex)->unlock();" in /clientDataset.C
  to avoid error deleting a mutex

* In Tcl files: replaced 'info objects' with 'itcl_info objects'

* In Tcl files, removed calls to 'winfo command' (no longer supported, 
  not needed).

* Added code to  dhsQlTool/dhsOcsWish.tcl to strip the "0x" off of the
  return value from "gethostid" (solaris just prints out the hex value
  without the 0x)

* Replaced the mixed sh/tcl script dhsQlTool-backend with two scripts:
  dhsQlTool (sh) and dhsQlTool-backend.tcl (tcl), since the original
  produced some errors on exit under Linux.

* In the dhsClient package: added htonl() wrapper on IP address in 
  dhs/connect.c, since the bytes were reversed.
